The nine UI01 files originally matched the applied Root bytes. SDK A03/A07 `contractId?`, A08/A09 required `contractId`, canonical optional `contractReadinessPackageId`, and strict B result fields match the current generated client. Correction02 fixes the real app→SDK boundary imports and three new assertions; correction03 supplies the actual ContractApi token mock and explicit-selection fixtures. No further compiler finding is claimed beyond Root's actual lint/build results.

The original pre-signing page has no A01/A05/A04 authoring editor. Upstream source production remains Root's real API chain; this batch displays its safe typed terms/seeds and executes A08/B/A09. Browser validation still needs two-contract selection, late-response behavior, masked projections, prepared version versus snapshot version, binding mismatch, correct sourceReadinessId reload, and UTC/Tokyo calendar dates. Static source review is not browser acceptance.
